# What NOT to upload when deploying the dashboard.
#
# This repository is ~2.2 GB, almost all of it market data: `data/` alone is
# 1.9 GB of session CSVs and the research archive. Vercel uploads the whole
# root as build context, so without this file the deploy either fails outright
# or takes many minutes for a dashboard that needs none of it.
#
# The dashboard reads its data from Atlas at runtime. The only local code it
# needs is `dashboard/` and the `algotrade` package (1.6 MB, 21 modules, no
# polars/pandas/duckdb -- those belong to the signals path, which the
# dashboard never touches).
#
# Deny-list rather than allow-list, deliberately: a missed allow rule fails at
# import time on the deployed function, which is a slow and confusing way to
# find out. A missed deny rule only wastes upload bandwidth.

# --- the 1.9 GB ------------------------------------------------------------
data/
backups/
reports/

# --- not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------
docs/
claude_fixes/
scripts/
tests/
jobs/
.github/

# The ROOT `config/` holds the frozen strategy YAML and the cost card, read by
# the signal path only. Anchored with a leading slash: written as `config/` it
# matched at any depth and silently removed `algotrade/config/` too, so the
# deployed function had no `algotrade.config` package and failed at import.
/config/

# The TRADING system's dependencies -- polars, pandas, duckdb, pyarrow,
# nsefin. Excluded so Vercel cannot resolve dependencies from it: the four the
# dashboard actually needs are declared in pyproject.toml, and installing this
# set would threaten the 500 MB function bundle limit for no benefit.
# GitHub Actions still reads it from git, which is unaffected by this file.
requirements.txt

# --- local development -----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
